git-svn-id: https://svn.apache.org/repos/asf/hadoop/common/trunk@1379100 13f79535-47bb-0310-9956-ffa450edef68

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the inability of MapReduce tasks to access the secrets stored in the `Credentials` object. The previous implementation used a method that only added tokens to the `UserGroupInformation` (UGI) instance, which did not include the secrets. This oversight meant that any secrets required for task execution were not available, leading to failures when tasks attempted to access these secrets.

Here is the patch:
